    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d442">

                <pb facs="0620" n="521" sameAs="frus:frus1936v05/pg521"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">822.5151/296</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Minister in Ecuador</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Gonzalez</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 164</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1936-08-14">August 14, 1936</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to your telegram No. 39, July 31,
                    11 a.m.,<anchor n="41" xml:id="d442-f1"/> the Department transmits a copy of an
                        <hi rendition="#italic">aide-mémoire</hi> handed to the Ecuadoran Minister
                    in Washington by Assistant Secretary of State, Mr. Welles, during the course of
                    a conversation upon the new Ecuadoran exchange control regulations. The <hi
                        rendition="#italic">aide-mémoire</hi> is for your information <pb
                        facs="0621" n="522" xml:id="pg522"/> only and the Department does not desire
                    to have you discuss the subject with the Ecuadoran authorities in the absence of
                    further instructions.</p>
                <p>Very truly yours,</p>
                <closer>For the Secretary of State:<lb/><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sumner
                            Welles</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
